__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,_e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(_e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(_e,"default",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return l}});var e,t=r(d[0]),o=(e=t)&&e.__esModule?e:{default:e},n=r(d[1]),s=r(d[2]);function l(){return(0,s.jsxs)(o.default,{title:"Terms of Service",path:"/terms",version:n.TERMS_VERSION,testID:"legal-terms",children:[(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"1. Who we are and what these terms cover",children:(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["HydroPass is operated by ",n.ENTITY_NAME," (",n.POSTAL_ADDRESS,"), called \"HydroPass\", \"we\" or \"us\" here. These terms are an agreement between you and us for using the HydroPass website and apps. By creating an account or making or accepting a booking, you agree to them, to our"," ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"/privacy",children:"Privacy Policy"})," and to our ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"/content-policy",children:"Content Policy"}),"."]})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"2. HydroPass is a marketplace",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"HydroPass lets landowners and others with the right to do so (\"hosts\") list access to land and water, and lets people (\"renters\") book it. We are not a party to the stay itself. We do not own, operate, manage, inspect or control any listed property, we are not the host, and we do not guide, supervise or provide any activity. Each booking is an agreement between the renter and the host. We do not guarantee the condition, safety, legality or suitability of any property, or the accuracy of any listing, review or message."})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"3. Your account",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:[`You must be at least ${n.MIN_AGE} years old and able to enter a binding contract to create an account, book or host.`,"Give accurate information and keep it current. One person per account; don't share your login.","You are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us at once if you think someone else has used it.","We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or puts others at risk."]})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"4. Booking as a renter",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["When you pick dates we hold the price for 15 minutes while you send your request. The host then approves or declines it.","Nothing is charged when you send a request. Once the host approves, you pay from your Pass. The price you see is the total: the nightly price times the number of nights, with no booking fee added to it.","The exact location, gate codes and access details are shared once your booking is paid. Use them only for your booking, and don't share them.","Follow the host's rules for the property (group size, vehicles, pets, fishing methods, catch-and-release, arrival and departure times) and everything the listing says."]})}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.Section,{heading:"5. Outdoor activities: your risks and your responsibilities",children:[(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"Fishing, wading, swimming, boating, camping and outdoor events carry real risks, including drowning, cold water, fast or rising water, slippery and uneven ground, wildlife, insects, weather, fire, and the condition of the land, roads and any structures. Help can be far away. By booking, you accept these risks for yourself and for everyone in your group, and you are responsible for your group, including any minors you bring."}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["Judge conditions for yourself, and don't go in or on the water, or start an activity, if it isn't safe.","Bring and use the right safety gear (for example life jackets on the water).","Follow the law: fishing licenses and stamps, seasons, size and bag limits, boating rules, fire restrictions and burn bans, and local rules.","Stay within the property's boundaries; don't enter neighboring land.","Leave the property as you found it, and report any damage to the host."]})]}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.Section,{heading:"6. Hosting",children:[(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"If you list a property, you promise and agree that:"}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["You own the property or otherwise have the legal right to rent access to it for the activities you list, and doing so doesn't break a lease, an HOA or deed restriction, a mortgage, a conservation easement or any other agreement.","You have, and will keep, every permit, license and registration that renting it requires, and you follow zoning, health, fire and safety rules.","Your listing is accurate, including its location, what is allowed and the price, and you keep its availability up to date.","You disclose known hazards that a renter couldn't easily see for themselves (for example deep or fast water, drop-offs, dams, old wells, unstable banks, livestock, hunting nearby).","You are responsible for insurance for your property and for the activities you allow. [[INSURANCE: state whether hosts are required to carry liability insurance, and how much, or that it is strongly recommended]]","You are responsible for any taxes due on what you earn, including any lodging or occupancy tax that applies to your property.","You honor confirmed bookings and the cancellation policy you chose, and you don't ask renters to pay you outside HydroPass."]}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["Payouts are handled by Stripe. To receive them you open a connected account with Stripe and agree to Stripe's own terms (the"," ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"https://stripe.com/connect-account/legal",children:"Stripe Connected Account Agreement"}),", which includes the Stripe Services Agreement), presented during onboarding. You authorize us to give Stripe information about you and your bookings, and to have Stripe pay you the booking total less our service fee."]})]}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"7. Prices, fees and payment",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["Renters pay the listed price for the nights booked. HydroPass adds no renter fee.","Hosts pay HydroPass a service fee, currently 10% of the booking total, taken from the payout. A promotion can lower it, as its own terms state.","Payments are processed by Stripe. We never see or store full card numbers.","If a tax or fee is ever added to a renter's price, it will be shown before you pay."]})}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.Section,{heading:"8. Cancellations and refunds",children:[(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"Each listing has one of four cancellation policies, shown on the listing and at checkout. A booking keeps the policy it was made under, even if the host changes the listing later. Days are counted in UTC from the booking's start date."}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["Flexible: full refund if the renter cancels at least 1 day before the stay; none after that.","Moderate: full refund at least 5 days before; half if cancelled at least 1 day before; none after that.","Strict: half refunded if cancelled at least 14 days before; none after that.","Non-refundable: no refund if the renter cancels."]}),(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"When a renter cancels, the refund is the policy's share of what was paid, less the same share of the card processing fee Stripe charged. A renter who hasn't paid yet can cancel at no charge. When a host cancels a paid booking, the renter gets a full refund and the host is charged the processing fee, taken from that payout or, if it doesn't cover it, from the host's next payouts. Nobody can cancel once a stay has ended. Refunds usually reach the card in 5 to 10 business days."})]}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"9. Reviews",children:(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["After a stay ends, the renter and the host can each review the other, once per booking. Only people who were part of a real booking can leave one, and you can't review yourself. We don't pay for reviews, offer anything for a good one, or hide or remove a review because it is negative. Nothing in these terms stops you from posting an honest review. We may remove a review that breaks the"," ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"/content-policy",children:"Content Policy"})," (for example one that is fake, threatening, reveals someone's private information or is about something other than the stay)."]})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"10. Your content",children:(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["You keep ownership of the photos, listings, reviews and messages you post. You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to host, show, copy, adapt (for example resize) and distribute that content to run and promote HydroPass, for as long as it is on HydroPass and for a reasonable time after. You promise you have the rights to what you post and that it follows the"," ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"/content-policy",children:"Content Policy"}),". Copyright complaints follow our"," ",(0,s.jsx)(t.A,{href:"/copyright",children:"Copyright Policy"}),"."]})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"11. Things you may not do",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.Bullets,{items:["Break the law, or use HydroPass to harm, harass, defraud or discriminate against anyone.","Take payment for a HydroPass booking outside HydroPass, or use HydroPass to find someone and then book around it.","List property you don't have the right to rent, or post false or misleading listings or reviews.","Scrape, copy or overload the service, get around its security, or access another person's account."]})}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.Section,{heading:"12. Disclaimers and limitation of liability",children:[(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"HydroPass is provided \"as is\" and \"as available\". To the fullest extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement, and we are not responsible for the acts or omissions of hosts, renters or anyone else, or for the condition of any property."}),(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"To the fullest extent the law allows, HydroPass is not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for personal injury, property damage or lost profits, arising from your use of HydroPass or from any stay or activity, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the greater of the fees HydroPass received for the booking concerned and $100. Some places don't allow some of these limits, so they may not all apply to you."}),(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"You agree to indemnify HydroPass against claims by others arising from your listing, your stay, your content or your breach of these terms."})]}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.Section,{heading:"13. Disputes and governing law",children:[(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["These terms are governed by the laws of the State of ",n.GOVERNING_STATE,", without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. [[DISPUTE RESOLUTION: the user decides whether to add an arbitration clause and class-action waiver, or name the courts of ",n.GOVERNING_STATE,"; attorney drafts this section]]"]}),(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:["If you have a problem with a booking, contact the other party first through HydroPass messages. If that doesn't solve it, write to us at ",(0,s.jsx)(t.Mail,{address:n.LEGAL_EMAIL}),"."]})]}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"14. Changes to these terms",children:(0,s.jsx)(t.P,{children:"We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version. If a change is material, we will tell you before it takes effect and ask you to accept the new terms before you book or host again; a change won't apply to a booking already confirmed under the old terms."})}),(0,s.jsx)(t.Section,{heading:"15. Contact",children:(0,s.jsxs)(t.P,{children:[n.ENTITY_NAME,", ",n.POSTAL_ADDRESS,". Email: ",(0,s.jsx)(t.Mail,{address:n.LEGAL_EMAIL}),"."]})})]})}},1221,[1063,909,625]);
